<attribute name="presentationName" nodeId="a106a2b5">Burndown Chart</attribute>
<attribute name="briefDescription" nodeId="ab69e3b6"></attribute>
<attribute name="suppressed" nodeId="8da4423">false</attribute>
<attribute name="orderingGuide" nodeId="82ab338a"></attribute>
<attribute name="authors" nodeId="5d936e9b"></attribute>
<attribute name="changeDate" nodeId="c94c4e8e"></attribute>
<attribute name="changeDescription" nodeId="355a79e7"></attribute>
<attribute name="version" nodeId="41a53da7"></attribute>
<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="d2ea6cb7"></attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="5bcc92d5"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="46010cf3">&lt;p&gt;
    The Burndown Chart:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Does not indicate scope changes to items
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Can provide insight on trends such as progress of work but does not provide details on partially complete work
        items
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Cannot calculate expected cost or budget overruns but can indicate the trajectory of the team
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Can be maintained in a digital format for ease of collaboration and communication
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Should be updated as soon as work is completed, this is done automatically if using an Agile tracking tool, or at a
        minimum during the daily scrum meeting for sprint level Burndown Charts 
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                An outdated Burndown Chart can prevent the team from understanding their actual progress against ideal
                burndown, which ultimately informs the team whether they are on track for the current sprint
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Release level Burndown Charts need only be updated once per sprint, at the end
            &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="cd4fdec"></attribute>
<attribute name="usageGuidance" nodeId="43c0bbc9"></attribute>
<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="cf013212">&lt;p&gt;
    A Burndown Chart is a graphical representation to track work completed by the team against the work planned for a given
    sprint. The graph displays all of the work planned as well as remaining (Y axis) on any given day of the sprint (X
    axis). The chart will show less and less work remaining as the team progresses and completes work. The chart empowers
    the team to own and visualize the plan thereby allowing them to manage any difficulties earlier and more decisively.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    The Burndown Chart also has a line to represent the &quot;ideal burndown&quot;. This indicates the ideal scenario where work
    would be completed at a uniform pace throughout the course of the sprint. Once the sprint is complete, the Burndown
    Chart is a catalog of patterns on observed performance. Compiled over time the Burndown Charts become an extensive
    history of past performance.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    The chart contains information on the:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Dynamics of the sprint&lt;/strong&gt; - such as the pace of work, discoveries made and the impact of adding work
        to the sprint in the case where the team is running ahead of schedule
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Current progress&lt;/strong&gt; - toward achieving the goal outlined for the sprint
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Need to adjust&lt;/strong&gt; - such as changes to the sprint goal&amp;nbsp;or removing impediments to speed up
        progress
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Finally, progress for an entire release can also be documented and tracked&amp;nbsp;via a Burndown Chart at the release
    level. The key differences between sprint and release level Burndown Charts are as follows:&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table title=&quot;&quot; style=&quot;HEIGHT: 234px; WIDTH: 466px&quot; cellspacing=&quot;0&quot; cellpadding=&quot;2&quot; width=&quot;466&quot; border=&quot;1&quot;&gt;
    &lt;tbody&gt;
        &lt;tr&gt;
            &lt;th scope=&quot;col&quot; abbr=&quot;&quot;&gt;
            &lt;/th&gt;
            &lt;th scope=&quot;col&quot; abbr=&quot;&quot;&gt;
                Sprint Burndown Chart
            &lt;/th&gt;
            &lt;th scope=&quot;col&quot; abbr=&quot;&quot;&gt;
                Release Burndown Chart
            &lt;/th&gt;
        &lt;/tr&gt;
        &lt;tr&gt;
            &lt;th scope=&quot;row&quot; abbr=&quot;&quot;&gt;
                X axis
            &lt;/th&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                Days
            &lt;/td&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                #&amp;nbsp;of Sprints
            &lt;/td&gt;
        &lt;/tr&gt;
        &lt;tr&gt;
            &lt;th scope=&quot;row&quot; abbr=&quot;&quot;&gt;
                Y axis
            &lt;/th&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                &lt;ul&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Story points sum,
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Ideal Days, or
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        # of Tasks
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;/ul&gt;
            &lt;/td&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                &lt;ul class=&quot;noindent&quot;&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Story points sum,
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Ideal Days, or
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        # of Backlog Items
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;/ul&gt;
            &lt;/td&gt;
        &lt;/tr&gt;
        &lt;tr&gt;
            &lt;th scope=&quot;row&quot; abbr=&quot;&quot;&gt;
                Update Frequency
            &lt;/th&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                As work is completed or at least daily
            &lt;/td&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                Updated once per sprint, at the end
            &lt;/td&gt;
        &lt;/tr&gt;
        &lt;tr&gt;
            &lt;th scope=&quot;row&quot; abbr=&quot;&quot;&gt;
                Inputs
            &lt;/th&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                Sprint Backlog estimates
            &lt;/td&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                Product Backlog estimates
            &lt;/td&gt;
        &lt;/tr&gt;
    &lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;</attribute>
</Element>
